  "prompt": "What penalties apply to late filing of a VAT return?",
  "runtimeCommit": "b7e40fc2af25db1c9eebbb23d1d537b3ec4bf1c8",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nPenalties for late filing of a VAT return include a fine of not less than One Thousand Pesos (₱1,000) but not more than Twenty-Five Thousand Pesos (₱25,000), and/or imprisonment of not less than six months but not more than two years, as stipulated under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practice, this means that businesses and individuals must ensure timely filing of their VAT returns to avoid incurring significant penalties. The risk of both financial penalties and imprisonment serves as a strong incentive for compliance with tax regulations.",
